Subject: [PATCH 11075/11362] Correct the induce note: that run used both GPUs,
 not GPU 1

The note's setup line says GPU 1. The run was launched with
CARNOT_ARC_GENERATOR_CUDA_GPU=1 but its llama-server appeared on both cards under
one pid, 10,542 and 11,364 MiB at about 50% each, visible in the 01:35Z and
02:35Z hourly checks. So its 31-38 tok/s decode and 6h57m wall-clock are
dual-card numbers and a single-card reproduction should not expect them.

Scoped deliberately rather than corrected wholesale. The 2026-09-03 tools A/B was
genuinely single-card -- GPU 0 read 4 MiB throughout both arms -- so the 2,496 MiB
arm-ON/arm-OFF delta and the note that it left 1,155 MiB against a 1,500 MiB guard
margin stand as recorded. Only the induce run was dual-card, and saying so
precisely matters more than a blanket retraction.

Records why it went unnoticed for a day: the dashboard prints per-GPU totals
rather than per-process ownership, so one server holding both cards is
indistinguishable from two jobs holding one each, and I read the line I expected.
It surfaced only when GPU 1 showed full utilisation at a moment I knew I had
nothing running.

